.TH ALIAS 1 "2026-04-12" "alias repo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alias \- portable shell configuration: aliases, git shortcuts, Pi helpers, jump navigation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source ~/.zshrc
.br
.B source ~/.bashrc
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B alias
repo is a set of shell configuration files for zsh and bash, designed to run identically on
macOS and Raspberry Pi (Debian/Ubuntu).
It provides general-purpose aliases, git shortcuts, Raspberry Pi SSH/SFTP helpers, a
directory-jump function, and interactive network tools.
.PP
Files are deployed by
.B deploy.sh
which symlinks dotfiles under
.I ~/
and auto-detects your shell.
Once sourced, all commands below are available in every new shell.
.SH NAMING CONVENTION
Every alias follows the pattern
.BR "<hw><action>[<addr>]>" .
.SS Hardware prefix
.TP
.B ra
Raspberry Pi
.TP
.B mc
Mac (uses
.I ~/.ssh/id_rsa
and Bonjour
.I .local
names)
.TP
.B pc
Windows PC (uses
.I ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
and domain
.IR ssb8 )
.TP
.B sy
Synology NAS (fixed host
.IR 192.168.1.116 )
.SS Action
.TP
.B p
SSH interactive session (heritage: PuTTY)
.TP
.B pp
SSH without key (password auth)
.TP
.B c
Run command(s) via SSH
.TP
.B w
SFTP interactive session (heritage: WinSCP)
.TP
.BR wl / wg / wu / wmk / wrm
SFTP non-interactive: list / get / put / mkdir / rm
.SS Address suffix (ra and pc only)
.TP
(none)
.I 192.168.1.<octet>
\(em by IP last octet
.TP
.B v
.IR <host>.ssb8.local " \(em Vienna DNS"
.TP
.B a
.IR <host>.pi.hole " \(em Aigen DNS"
.PP
.B mc
uses
.IR <name>.local " (Bonjour) \(em no octet/v/a suffix."
.B sy
has a fixed host \(em no address suffix.
.SH INSTALL
.B One-line install:
.PP
.RS
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/refap3/alias/master/install.sh | bash
.RE
.PP
.B Update (once installed):
.PP
.RS
alu
.RE
.PP
.B Deploy options:
.PP
.RS
./deploy.sh [\-\-shell zsh|bash] [\-\-home | \-\-path <dir>]
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I alias.zsh
General aliases and functions loaded at every shell start.
.TP
.I gitalias.zsh
Git shortcuts. Loaded at login; unload with
.BR sl ,
reload with
.BR gital .
.TP
.I raspberryalias.zsh
SSH/SFTP aliases for Raspberry Pi hosts (by IP octet or hostname) and Windows PC PowerShell remoting and remote command execution.
.TP
.I synologyalias.zsh
SSH/SFTP aliases for the Synology NAS (fixed host 192.168.1.116, user pipi).
.TP
.I jump.sh
.BR cd (1)
