.SS Docker Compose
All
.I dc*
commands auto-detect the compose plugin
.RI ( "docker compose" )
or fall back to
.IR docker-compose .
They also auto-detect
.I docker-compose.yml
vs
.I compose.yml
in the given folder.
.TP
.B dcu " [folder]"
docker compose up
.TP
.B dcud " [folder]"
docker compose up -d (detached)
.TP
.B dcd " [folder]"
docker compose down
.TP
.B dcde " [folder]"
docker compose down and erase everything: all images
.RB ( --rmi " all),"
volumes
.RB ( --volumes ),
orphaned containers
.RB ( --remove-orphans ).
Use this for a complete clean slate.
.TP
.B dcinfo " [-v] [name]"
List all containers (running and stopped).
.I name
is an optional substring/regex filter applied to container names.
Without
.BR -v :
prints one line per container with name, status, image, and ports.
With
.BR -v :
prints full
.BR "docker inspect"
JSON for each matched container.
.TP
.B dclog " [name] [nn]"
Show the last
.I nn
log lines for each container whose name matches
.IR name .
If
.I name
is omitted, all containers are shown.
If the first argument is an integer, it is treated as
.I nn
and all containers are shown.
If
.I nn
is
.BR 0 ,
the entire log is shown.
If
.I nn
is omitted, the last 10 lines are shown.
