.SS Cloudflare Tunnel Client
.B rap59cv
and
.B rap168ca
use
.I cloudflared access ssh
as an SSH ProxyCommand.
The Mac has
.I cloudflared
via Homebrew.
Any Pi that calls these aliases must also have
.I cloudflared
installed.
.PP
Install on an aarch64 (64-bit) Pi:
.PP
.nf
curl -fsSL https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared/releases/latest/\\
download/cloudflared-linux-arm64.deb -o /tmp/cloudflared.deb
sudo dpkg -i /tmp/cloudflared.deb
.fi
.PP
For a 32-bit (armv7) Pi replace
.I arm64
with
.IR arm .
Check with
.B uname -m
.RI ( aarch64 " = arm64," " armv7l" " = arm)."
.SH WINDOWS PC ALIASES
SSH-based interactive PowerShell and remote command execution for Windows PCs.
Uses
.I ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
(not id_rsa), domain
.IR ssb8 ,
user
.IR rainer .
Requires OpenSSH server and PowerShell 7 on the Windows PC.
.SS Interactive PowerShell (pcp)
Connects via SSH and starts
.B pwsh
on the remote Windows PC, sourcing
.B $profile.CurrentUserAllHosts
on startup.
.TP
.B pcp " <octet>"
SSH to
.I 192.168.1.<octet>
as
.I rainer
and start an interactive
.B pwsh
session.
.TP
.B pcpv " <host>"
SSH to
.I <host>.ssb8.local
as
.I rainer
and start an interactive
.B pwsh
session.
.TP
.B pcpa " <host>"
SSH to
.I <host>.pi.hole
as
.I rainer
and start an interactive
.B pwsh
session.
.SS Remote Command Execution
Commands are piped to
.B pwsh
via SSH (analogous to
.B rac
for Pis).
Requires OpenSSH server on Windows with
.I pwsh.exe
set as the default shell.
.TP
.B pcc " <octet[,octet]> <cmd>"
Run a PowerShell command on one Windows PC (by IP octet) or multiple (comma-separated).
.TP
.B pccv " <host[,host]> <cmd>"
Run a PowerShell command on one or more Windows PCs by
.I .ssb8.local
hostname.
.TP
.B pcca " <host[,host]> <cmd>"
Run a PowerShell command on one or more Windows PCs by
.I .pi.hole
hostname.
.SS SFTP / SCP
.TP
.B pcw " <octet>"
Interactive SFTP to Windows PC by IP octet.
.TP
.B pcwv " <host>"
Interactive SFTP to
.IR rainer@<host>.ssb8.local .
.TP
.B pcwa " <host>"
Interactive SFTP to
.IR rainer@<host>.pi.hole .
.TP
.B pcwl " <octet> [dir]"
List remote directory.
.TP
.B pcwg " <octet> <remote> [local]"
Download file or directory from Windows PC (scp -r).
.TP
.B pcwu " <octet> <local> [remote]"
Upload file or directory to Windows PC (scp -r).
.TP
.B pcwmk " <octet> <dir>"
Create directory on Windows PC.
.TP
.B pcwrm " <octet> <path>"
Remove file on Windows PC (prompts for confirmation first).
.TP
.B pcwh
Show Windows PC SFTP one-liner help.
.PP
All
.I pcwl/pcwg/pcwu/pcwmk/pcwrm
commands have
.BR v " and " a
variants (e.g.
.BR pcwlv ,
.BR pcwla )
for
.I .ssb8.local
and
.I .pi.hole
