.SS Windows OpenSSH Setup (run once on the Windows Server, elevated PowerShell)
.TP
1.
Install and enable OpenSSH Server:
.RS
.I Add-WindowsCapability -Online -Name OpenSSH.Server~~~~0.0.1.0
.br
.I Start-Service sshd
.br
.I Set-Service -Name sshd -StartupType 'Automatic'
.RE
.TP
2.
Set PowerShell 7 as the SSH default shell:
.RS
.I New-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\OpenSSH" -Name DefaultShell -Value "C:\Program Files\PowerShell\7\pwsh.exe" -PropertyType String -Force
.RE
.TP
3.
Add Mac's public key to
.IR authorized_keys :
.RS
For regular users:
.I $HOME\\.ssh\\authorized_keys
.br
For Administrator:
.I C:\ProgramData\ssh\administrators_authorized_keys
.br
Fix ACL:
.I icacls "$HOME\\.ssh\\authorized_keys" /inheritance:r /grant "${env:USERNAME}:(R)" /grant "SYSTEM:(R)"
.RE
.SS New Mac Setup
.TP
1.
Install PowerShell 7:
.RS
.I curl -L -o /tmp/pwsh.pkg "https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases/download/v7.6.0/powershell-7.6.0-osx-arm64.pkg"
.br
.I sudo installer -pkg /tmp/pwsh.pkg -target /
.RE
.TP
2.
Generate or copy the ed25519 key:
.RS
.I ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "rainers@mac" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.br
Or copy from an existing Mac:
.I scp mm:~/.ssh/id_ed25519{,.pub} ~/.ssh/ && chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.RE
.TP
3.
Add key to the macOS keychain:
.RS
.I ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.RE
.TP
4.
Ensure
.I ~/.ssh/config
has a host-specific entry for each Windows host to override the Pi wildcard (which uses id_rsa):
.RS
.I Host es.ssb8.local
.br
.I "    "IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
.RE
