.SH JUMP FUNCTION
The
.B cd
command is wrapped to record every visited directory into
.IR ~/.jumplocations .
.TP
.B j " <partial-name>"
Jump to a previously visited directory by partial folder name (case-insensitive).
If multiple matches are found, an interactive numbered menu is shown.
.TP
.B j -d
Remove the current directory from the jump cache.
.TP
.B j -dr
Remove the current directory and all subdirectories from the jump cache.
.SH NETWORK TOOLS
.B nw
launches an interactive menu with the following tools:
.PP
.TS
l l.
1	IPv4 addresses
i	IPv6 addresses
2	IPv4 full details (interfaces, routes, DNS)
j	IPv6 full details
3	Release DHCP lease
4	Renew DHCP lease
5	Flush DNS cache
6	Show ARP/neighbour table
7	Clear ARP table
8	Ping default gateway
9	Ping 8.8.8.8 (internet check)
a	Traceroute to host
b	DNS lookup (A/AAAA/MX/NS/TXT)
c	Routing table
d	Active/listening ports
e	External / public IP
f	Port test (nc -zv)
g	WiFi interface details
h	Wake-on-LAN (lists known hosts with online/MAC status; pick by number or enter manually)
k	Interface summary table
l	Bandwidth test (latency + download speed)
0	Exit
.TE
.PP
Run as
.B nw <choice>
to execute a single tool non-interactively and exit.
Missing tools show a clear error with the
.I apt install
command rather than silently failing.
.SH CLAUDE CODE ALIASES
.TP
.B cdsp
Launch Claude Code with
.I --dangerously-skip-permissions
(bypasses all permission prompts).
.TP
.B csess
Generate a session report for the current project (claudeExperiments) and open the interactive HTML in the browser.
Outputs
.I sessions_YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM.md
and
.I sessions_YYYY-MM-DD_HHMM.html
to
.IR ~/.dotfiles/sessions/ .
Each session includes an AI-generated one-line description (in the summary bar) and a 3\(en5 sentence paragraph (in the expanded panel), produced by
.B claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
and cached in
.IR ~/.dotfiles/sessions/summaries_cache.json .
Requires
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
in the environment or saved to
.IR ~/.config/anthropic/api_key .
Pass
.B \-\-no\-summaries
to skip API calls entirely.
.TP
.B csessall
Same as
.B csess
but covers all Claude Code projects on this machine.
